A live-action ''[[Star Wars]]'' '''film''' was planned to be released on [[December 18]], [[2026]], but was later removed from [[The Walt Disney Company|Disney]]'s release slate. The film was revealed on [[June 13]], [[2023]] after the start of the [[Wikipedia:2023 Writers Guild of America strike|2023 Writers Guild of America strike]] when Disney re-organized their theatrical film release slate.<ref name="WGA">{{WebCite|url=https://deadline.com/2023/06/disney-marvel-wga-strike-thunderbolts-blade-avengers-kang-dynasty-1235415782|text='Thunderbolts', 'Blade', 'Avengers: Kang Dynasty', 'Secret Wars' Among Disney Release Date Changes Due To WGA Strike|author=Anthony D'Alessandro|date=2023-06-13|work=[[Wikipedia:Deadline Hollywood|''Deadline'']]|archivedate=20230613153245}}</ref> In the [[2024]] Q3 Earnings Presentation on [[August 7]], Disney confirmed its commitment to releasing [[Star Wars: The Mandalorian and Grogu|''The Mandalorian and Grogu'']] and a second film in [[2026]], along with [[Star Wars: Starfighter|another film]] in [[2027]].<ref name="2024 Q3 Call">{{DisneyCompany|url=/app/uploads/2024/08/Q3-FY24-Earnings-Presentation.pdf|text=Q3 FY24 Earnings Presentation}}</ref> On [[November 15]], [[2024]], Disney released an updated release schedule for its theatrical films, pulling the untitled ''Star Wars'' film off its calendar and instead giving the release date slot to the forthcoming animated film [[Wikipedia:Ice Age 6|''Ice Age 6'']].<ref name="Canceled">{{WebCite|url=https://deadline.com/2024/11/star-wars-movie-unset-ice-age-6-1236178369|text='Star Wars' Holiday 2026 Movie Unset, Disney Backfills With 'Ice Age 6'|author=Anthony D'Alessandro|date=2024-11-15|work=[[Wikipedia:Deadline Hollywood|''Deadline'']]|archivedate=20241225121108}}</ref>

